# APCTT common base environment: the input of requirements-base.lock (decisions D60, D64 and D67,
# 2026-10-10).
#
# One fixed base for every team, with no per-team packages (D64): the D52 PyTorch closure (torch
# 2.11.0+cu128 and its CUDA 12.8 packages, exact pins) plus a curated set of common packages whose
# licences the policy allows. Target: Linux x86_64, CPython 3.12. The organizer installs it once per
# evaluation machine, read-only, and every team's worker runs its python; public models come from
# the model catalogue (contracts/model-catalog.json). Teams build the same base with
# tools/make_env.py and do not ship or redistribute it.
#
# torch comes from the PyTorch cu128 page (--find-links https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128/torch/),
# everything else from PyPI. overrides-base.txt keeps opencv-python out (opencv-python-headless
# provides cv2). The organizer re-locks only by decision; the lock, constraints-base.txt and
# contracts/base-environment.json change together.

